## 6. Installation on Windows

1. Download the STOCKWISE project ZIP.
2. Extract the ZIP file.
3. Open the project folder.
4. Double-click setup_and_run.bat.
5. Wait for the required packages to install.
6. The Flask backend will start.

Open your browser and visit:

http://127.0.0.1:5000

Keep the terminal open while using the application.

If Python is not installed, install Python 3.10 or later.
During Windows installation, select "Add Python to PATH".

---

## 7. Manual Installation Using VS Code

Open the STOCKWISE folder in VS Code.

Open Terminal > New Terminal.

Create a virtual environment:

    py -m venv .venv

Activate the environment:

    .venv\Scripts\activate

Install dependencies:

    py -m pip install -r requirements.txt

Start the backend:

    py app.py

Open the website:

    http://127.0.0.1:5000

Do not open index.html directly for this Python edition.
Use the Flask server address.

